From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ims-config: send the identity tags stock sends

Decoding `AIMS_HIDDEN_MENU` out of five same-day Android boots on this
baseband with these SIMs puts an exact number on what we were missing.
Stock sends 80 tags on the Telus stack and 81 on the Videotron one; we
sent 77 on both, and the four it has that we lack are all in the device
identity block:

    777   int 1       both stacks, both carriers, 5/5 boots
    778   string      the IMS home domain -- Videotron only
    782   string ""   both
    783   string ""   both

778 is conditional on the card, not the carrier: the Videotron card
carries an ISIM (AID A000000087 1004) and is sent
ims.mnc500.mcc302.3gppnetwork.org, the Telus card carries none and is
sent no domain at all. Both cards are in the capture, and the AID is in
it too, so this is read off the wire rather than guessed. The domain
itself is 3GPP TS 23.003 13.2, with the MNC padded to three digits --
which is why it cannot be made by splitting the MCCMNC in half.

The empty strings are sent rather than skipped because a tag absent from
the menu leaves the CP's slot holding whatever was in it; "" is a value,
not an omission.

Tag 773 also disagreed. The device tree says "Pixel 9 Pro XL" and stock
sends "Pixel9ProXL", in tag 773 and inside the User-Agent alike, so the
model token now drops its spaces instead of hyphenating them. Every other
User-Agent field still hyphenates: the captures show no model with spaces,
so there is nothing to copy for the rest.

With this the tag sets match exactly -- 80 for Telus, 81 for Videotron.
